{title: At Calvary (I Am Free)}
{artist: William Reed Newell, Daniel Brink Towner, C. Michael Pilato}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 98}

Verse 1
Years I spent in vanity and pride,
Caring not my Lord was crucified,
Knowing not it was for me He died on Calvary.

Verse 2
By God's Word at last my sin I learned,
Then I trembled at the law I'd spurned,
Till my guilty soul imploring turned to Calvary.

Chorus
Mercy there was great and grace was free.
Pardon there was multiplied to me.
There my burdened soul found liberty at Calvary!

Verse 3
Oh the love that drew salvation's plan!
Oh the grace that brought it down to man!
Oh the mighty gulf that God did span at Calvary!

Chorus
Mercy there was great and grace was free.
Pardon there was multiplied to me.
There my burdened soul found liberty at Calvary!

Verse 4
I am free.  I am free.
By the mercy of God's great grace, I am free.
I am free (and I am forgiven).  I am free (and now I am living).
By the mercy of God's great grace, I am free.

Verse 5
Now I give to Jesus everything.
Now I gladly own Him as my King.
Now my raptured soul can only sing of Calvary!
